==English==

===Etymology===
From {{prefix|anti|matter|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈæntimæˌtɚ/|/ˈæn.taɪ.mæˌtɚ/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# {{context|physics|lang=en}} [[matter|Matter]] that is composed of the [[antiparticle]]s of those that [[constitute]] normal matter.
# {{context|physics|lang=en}} A form of matter that has a key property, such as [[charge]], opposite to that of ordinary matter.

